# Canonical Orryx Group secret/PII .gitignore patterns
# Source of truth — appended to every repo's .gitignore in Wave 0 (2026-05-12)
# Maintained by: orryx-standards

# Secrets/credentials patterns
secrets-*.json
*-secrets.json
.secrets-staged.json
.env
.env.local
.env.production
.env.staging
.env.backup*
.env.bak
.env.old
.env.local-*
pilot_users.json
pilot-users.json

# --- .env* POLICY: NEVER add negations here (added 2026-07-30) ---
# Do NOT add `!.env.production` or `!.env.staging`. Only `!.env.example` is safe.
#
# Observed in the wild 2026-07-30: a generated ignore block in three repos
# (property-maintenance-os, orryx-delivery-dashboard, orryx-website) re-enabled
# these with the rationale "permits public Vite build config — client-inlined".
# That rationale does not survive contact with either framework:
#   - Next.js inlines ONLY `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`. A .env.production there routinely holds
#     server-side secrets (DB URLs, cloud keys, OAuth creds).
#   - Vite inlines ONLY `VITE_*`. A .env.production there can still carry
#     build-time secrets that never reach the client bundle.
# In both cases the negation force-tracks precisely the file most likely to hold
# credentials. Two of the three repos above are not even Vite projects.
#
# If a repo genuinely needs public build config committed, commit a distinctly
# named file (e.g. `public-build-config.json`) — never a `.env*` file. The name
# `.env` is what makes tooling, humans and future agents assume "secrets live here".

# Terraform state (often contains plaintext secrets)
terraform-state-backup-*.json
terraform-state-backup-$(*).json
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.backup
.terraform/

# Cloud access keys
*.privatekey
*-credentials.csv
*_credentials.csv
*-accessKeys.csv
*_accessKeys.csv
aws-credentials*
bedrock-*-keys*

# Cert/key files
*.pem
*.key
*.pfx
*.p12

# Deployment-doc leak vector (added 2026-05-17 — root cause of NEW-04/NEW-07:
# live env values repeatedly committed in summary/completion markdown)
*DEPLOYMENT_SUMMARY*.md
*DEPLOYMENT*COMPLETION*.md
*_COMPLETION.md
WEEK*_*.md

# Anti-pattern: failed shell-expansion filenames
*$(date*
*${date*

# OS artefacts (Windows)
NUL
nul
$RECYCLE.BIN/
